From: OPIZ3 br2-external
Subject: Bluetooth: hci_sync: do not request park in default link policy

UWE5622 advertises LMP park but rejects HCI_LP_PARK in
Write Default Link Policy Settings with status 0x12, failing hci0 init.
Park state is removed from the Bluetooth Core spec.
---
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
@@ -4117,8 +4117,6 @@
 		link_policy |= HCI_LP_HOLD;
 	if (lmp_sniff_capable(hdev))
 		link_policy |= HCI_LP_SNIFF;
-	if (lmp_park_capable(hdev))
-		link_policy |= HCI_LP_PARK;
 
 	cp.policy = cpu_to_le16(link_policy);
 
